{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/jvi9cp","slideIndex":0,"layout":{"id":"ly/a143ax0z","name":"Blank"},"title":"STUDY WITH NUDGE","textShapes":3,"backgroundColor":"rgba(38,61,53,1)"}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/9o3adcbe","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":76,"top":58,"width":1080,"height":34},"text":"STUDY WITH NUDGE","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":16,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#CBE2B7","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/mlcbixcn","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":76,"top":124,"width":1110,"height":152},"text":"Nudge","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":58,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#F7F7F1","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/nmlsb2t8","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":76,"top":328,"width":960,"height":78},"text":"A quiet companion for getting back to your work.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":34,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#F7F7F1","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/jvi9cp","slideIndex":0,"text":"0:00–0:20. “Students with ADHD can drift away from a task even when they want to do it. Nudge stays nearby and helps them return without judgment.” This is the product premise, not a measured outcome."}
{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/9kw6bv","slideIndex":1,"layout":{"id":"ly/a143ax0z","name":"Blank"},"title":"THE PROBLEM","textShapes":4,"backgroundColor":"rgba(247,247,241,1)"}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/d8jit8jm","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":76,"top":58,"width":1080,"height":34},"text":"THE PROBLEM","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":16,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#62796B","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/q5szidkv","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":76,"top":124,"width":1110,"height":152},"text":"Coming back is the hard part","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":58,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#263D35","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/r610ri1g","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":76,"top":322,"width":1060,"height":78},"text":"A break turns into a different tab.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":34,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#263D35","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/0bu1onid","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":76,"top":414,"width":1060,"height":78},"text":"The draft is still open. Restarting feels far away.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":34,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#62796B","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/9kw6bv","slideIndex":1,"text":"0:20–0:40. “Most focus tools try to stop a detour. We designed for the moment after one happens. Nudge keeps the student in control and makes the first step back small.”"}
{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/p2ae02","slideIndex":2,"layout":{"id":"ly/a143ax0z","name":"Blank"},"title":"LIVE DEMO","textShapes":6,"backgroundColor":"rgba(38,61,53,1)"}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/w3mtcbad","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":76,"top":58,"width":1080,"height":34},"text":"LIVE DEMO","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":16,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#CBE2B7","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/b2dcj69s","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":76,"top":124,"width":1110,"height":152},"text":"One essay. One detour. One return.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":58,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#F7F7F1","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/a14ba1s7","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":76,"top":322,"width":1060,"height":78},"text":"Google Docs essay","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":33,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#F7F7F1","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/lsfup0ru","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":76,"top":390,"width":1060,"height":78},"text":"YouTube detour","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":33,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#F7F7F1","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/kr6tgva9","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":76,"top":458,"width":1060,"height":78},"text":"“Take me back”","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":33,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#F7F7F1","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/jqxcnq9o","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":76,"top":526,"width":1060,"height":78},"text":"A question beside the draft","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":33,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#F7F7F1","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/p2ae02","slideIndex":2,"text":"0:40–2:00. Run the live demo from TASKS.md: save the history essay task, lock the Google Doc, type a sentence, switch to YouTube, wait for the nudge, say “Ugh, I’m stuck. Take me back,” then show the note beside the document. If the live path is not ready, do not imply it worked; use the backup recording after it has been captured."}
{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/qe97pd","slideIndex":3,"layout":{"id":"ly/a143ax0z","name":"Blank"},"title":"HOW IT WORKS","textShapes":5,"backgroundColor":"rgba(247,247,241,1)"}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/8vut0r2t","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":76,"top":58,"width":1080,"height":34},"text":"HOW IT WORKS","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":16,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#62796B","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/nuls7ml8","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":76,"top":124,"width":1110,"height":152},"text":"Quiet until help is useful","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":58,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#263D35","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/mtsbyhkn","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":76,"top":322,"width":1060,"height":78},"text":"Live screen context shows what changed.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":30,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#263D35","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/x03udw3a","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":76,"top":412,"width":1060,"height":78},"text":"App rules own the timer and grace period.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":30,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#263D35","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/wzut4r2p","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":76,"top":502,"width":1060,"height":78},"text":"A small prompt helps the student re-enter.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":30,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#263D35","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/qe97pd","slideIndex":3,"text":"2:00–2:25. “One Live session sees the screen, while deterministic rules decide when to check in. The model helps with the wording and the next step. The app keeps the timing, pause, and snooze controls.”"}
{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/96ihwx","slideIndex":4,"layout":{"id":"ly/a143ax0z","name":"Blank"},"title":"STUDENT CONTROL","textShapes":5,"backgroundColor":"rgba(247,247,241,1)"}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/9cnut0fa","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":76,"top":58,"width":1080,"height":34},"text":"STUDENT CONTROL","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":16,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#62796B","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/m9wbylwj","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":76,"top":124,"width":1110,"height":152},"text":"Support without pressure","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":58,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#263D35","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/na5srqx4","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":76,"top":320,"width":1060,"height":78},"text":"Pause or snooze in one action.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":32,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#263D35","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/07etwvet","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":76,"top":414,"width":1060,"height":78},"text":"Research and task related videos can count as work.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":32,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#263D35","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/18nap0fy","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":76,"top":508,"width":1060,"height":78},"text":"Next steps are questions, never assignment text.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":32,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#263D35","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/96ihwx","slideIndex":4,"text":"2:25–2:45. “Nudge never blocks a site or writes the assignment. The student can say a video is for the task, take a break, or turn the session off.”"}
{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/pqma7p","slideIndex":5,"layout":{"id":"ly/a143ax0z","name":"Blank"},"title":"NEXT","textShapes":4,"backgroundColor":"rgba(38,61,53,1)"}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/kjqtk7eh","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":76,"top":58,"width":1080,"height":34},"text":"NEXT","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":16,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#CBE2B7","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/zihcr2xw","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":76,"top":124,"width":1110,"height":152},"text":"A gentler way back","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":58,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#F7F7F1","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/yh8bixwb","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":76,"top":335,"width":1050,"height":78},"text":"Broader app support and stronger privacy controls are next.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":31,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#F7F7F1","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/9ojuxcfy","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":76,"top":438,"width":1050,"height":78},"text":"For now, we are proving one reliable study path.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":31,"typeface":"Helvetica Neue","color":"#CBE2B7","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/pqma7p","slideIndex":5,"text":"2:45–3:00. “We are starting with a Google Docs essay in Chrome. We want to expand to other workflows and give students clearer control over what the app sees and keeps.” Invite questions. Do not claim these future capabilities exist today."}